<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18387" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Flōrentĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Etruria</i>, <i>situated on the river
				Arno</i>, the modern <i>Florence</i>, <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 21
					<i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Front. de Colon. p. 112</span></i> Goes.; cf.
			Zumpt, de Colon. p. 253.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Flōrentĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a sort of
			vine</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 3, 4, §
			36</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Flōren-tīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Florentia</i>, <i>Florentine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Colonia,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Florentia</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Front.
				1</span></i>
			. 1.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Flō-rentīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Florentia</i>, <i>Florentines</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 8, § 52</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 1,
			79</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
